      "icon": {
        "file": "nativity-diptych-nmafa",
        "title": "The Nativity, with the Annunciation, the Magi and the life of Mary",
        "credit": "Ethiopia, 17th century · National Museum of African Art, Smithsonian, CC0"
      },
      "reviewStatus": "draft",
      "note": "ANSWERED 28 Sep 2026: begins Hidar 16, not 15. Ends where it always did, the day before Tsome Gahad on Tahsas 28, expressed as an endpoint rather than the old 43-day count so that moving the start cannot drag the end with it. Hidar 16 to Tahsas 27 is 42 days. UPDATED 15 Oct 2026 by the project owner: the fast runs through the eve of Genna (Tahsas 28, or 27 in the year after an Ethiopic leap year), so it always ends on 6 January, 43 days from Hidar 16. Before a Wednesday or Friday Genna the eve is also Tsome Gahad. This replaces the reviewer's end on Tahsas 27, and keeps the eve a fast day every year (the safety rule). ANSWERED on Review Sheet 4 (17 Oct 2026): the end is right, and the fast begins on Hidar 15, so it runs 24 November to 6 January (25 November after an Ethiopic leap year). ICON added 16 Oct 2026 at the owner's request (content/icons/CREDITS.md); Review Sheet 4: suitable."
    },
