      "reviewStatus": "draft",
      "note": "DECIDED 15 Oct 2026 by the project owner: Gahad is kept only when Genna falls on a Wednesday or Friday, and that Genna is then free of the fast (dispensation genna-feast). Review Sheet 4 (17 Oct 2026): the reviewer AGREES, withdrawing the earlier answers below as too broad. Earlier: 28 Sep they placed the end of Tsome Nebiyat on \"the day before Tsome Gahad on Tahsas 28\", reading Gahad as every year, and on Review Sheet 2 they said moving the fast to the eve \"only applies to Timket\". The eve is still a fast day every year, as the last day of Tsome Nebiyat (also decided 15 Oct 2026). Both confirmed on Review Sheet 4 (17 Oct 2026). Also 15 Oct 2026: Genna, this eve, the end of Tsome Nebiyat and genna-feast all move a day earlier in the year after an Ethiopic leap year, so Genna stays on 7 January; before this, 2028 and 2032 showed Genna on 8 January."
    },
